```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Long-horizon agents with high fact recurrence (>25% re-store rate) and queries that value old facts over recent ones; but only when threshold is tuned >=0.5 and paraphrase is low. MemGPT/Letta-style systems with archival memory might fit, but they already use importance-weighted eviction which is stronger than the size-cap baseline tested.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only. The >25% amplification holds only at re-store >=0.25 or saturated universe (packet L0: 0.197 at restore=0.2, below threshold). Dedup beats size-cap only with tuned threshold (thr0.5 +0.103 CI[+0.076,+0.130]; thr0.3 CI includes 0 and loses -0.31 in short-horizon). Win disappears under high paraphrase (gate recall 0.38-0.54), loose gate (precision 0.37), or short-horizon queries where recency suffices. Size-cap is a stronger baseline than assumed, tying/beating dedup in 18/108 configs.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Threshold is a knob requiring per-corpus tuning (not robust/free); Lexical Jaccard fails under paraphrase (oracle gap mean +0.12, max +0.80); Real systems (MemGPT/Letta) already implement importance/recency eviction, stronger than pure size-cap; No evidence from real agent logs that re-store rate exceeds 25%; Short-horizon conversational queries favor recency, making size-cap sufficient; Embedding-based gate adds cost/complexity, violating "cheap" claim]
RATIONALE: Packet L0 shows amplification is conditional (0.197 <25% at restore=0.2 with large universe, only 0.75 due to saturation artifact) and dedup win is threshold-sensitive (thr0.3 CI[-0.048,+0.072] includes 0; thr0.5+ required). Size-cap ties/beats dedup when gate is loose, paraphrase high, or horizon short (packet: "SIZE-CAP is a STRONGER baseline than the claim assumed — it ties/beats dedup whenever the gate is loose, paraphrase is high, or queries want recent facts"). Prior work (MemGPT/Letta, Generative-Agents) already manages eviction via importance/reflection (packet novelty_killer). Negative result is actionable: do not expect robust free win from content-dedup; size-cap is sufficient for many regimes; if dedup is used, threshold must be tuned and paraphrase will defeat lexical signals.
```
